  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expanding Rural Road Access to Foster Social Impact by Digitally Optimising Infrastructure Investments.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a flagship initiative within the UNIDO Programme for Country Partnership (PCP) for C&#xf4;te d#Ivoire, under Component IV: Inclusive and Sustainable Development of Territories and Rural Areas Based on the Development of Value Chains. It enables UNIDO to support addressing the challenges related to road infrastructure which continuously hinder industrial development and value chains. UNIDO#s intervention, leveraging its partnership with ORIS, addresses key challenges in road infrastructure by introducing a multidimensional, digitised approach to planning and development, and innovative financing mechanisms, powered by optimisation. Leveraging its expertise in technology transfer and capacity building, UNIDO will integrate advanced digital tools for more efficient design, construction, and maintenance of road networks. This intervention supports data-driven decision-making and optimises resource allocation, addressing gaps in local capacity while promoting climate-resilient infrastructure. The Roads4People project aligns with UNIDO#s mandate to promote inclusive and sustainable industrial development (ISID) by focusing on rural development, climate resilience, and digitalization. Furthermore, the project is fully aligned with UNIDO&apos;s 2022-2025 Medium-term Programme Framework (MTPF). By leveraging digit</narrative>
  </description>
